  "question": {
    "text": "A light source of wavelength $\\lambda$ illuminates a metal surface and electrons are ejected with maximum kinetic energy of 2 eV . If the same surface is illuminated by a light source of wavelength $\\frac{\\lambda}{2}$, then the maximum kinetic energy of ejected electrons will be (The work function of metal is 1 eV )",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5MvZc",
      "text": "3 eV",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FRklA",
      "text": "2 eV",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "uSqWm",
      "text": "6 eV",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XZit3",
      "text": "5 eV",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Einstein's photoelectric equation\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{KE}=\\frac{h c}{\\lambda}=\\phi_0 \\\\\n& 2 \\mathrm{eV}=\\frac{h c}{\\lambda}-1 \\mathrm{eV} \\\\\n& \\frac{h c}{\\lambda}=3 \\mathrm{eV} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{KE}^{\\prime}=\\frac{h c}{(\\lambda / 2)}-\\phi_0=6 \\mathrm{eV}-1 \\mathrm{eV}\n\\end{aligned}$\n$=5 \\mathrm{eV}$",
    "image": null
  },
